    solution: "public with sharing class TemplateMerger {\n    private static final Pattern TOKEN = Pattern.compile('\\\\{\\\\{\\\\s*([A-Za-z0-9_.]+)\\\\s*\\\\}\\\\}');\n\n    public static String merge(String template, Map<String, Object> values) {\n        if (template == null) return null;\n        Map<String, Object> lookup = new Map<String, Object>();\n        if (values != null) {\n            for (String key : values.keySet()) {\n                if (key != null) lookup.put(key.toLowerCase(), values.get(key));\n            }\n        }\n        Matcher m = TOKEN.matcher(template);\n        List<String> parts = new List<String>();\n        Integer last = 0;\n        while (m.find()) {\n            parts.add(template.substring(last, m.start()));\n            Object value = lookup.get(m.group(1).toLowerCase());\n            parts.add(value == null ? '' : formatValue(value));\n            last = m.end();\n        }\n        parts.add(template.substring(last));\n        return String.join(parts, '');\n    }\n\n    private static String formatValue(Object value) {\n        if (value instanceof Date) return ((Date) value).format();\n        return String.valueOf(value);\n    }\n}\n",
    checks: [{ re: /static\s+String\s+merge\s*\(\s*String\s+\w+\s*,\s*Map<\s*String\s*,\s*Object\s*>\s+\w+\s*\)/i, msg: "Keeps the required method signature" }, { re: /Pattern\.compile\(/i, msg: "Uses a compiled Pattern" }, { re: /\.find\(\)/i, msg: "Iterates matches with find()" }, { re: /toLowerCase\(\)|toUpperCase\(\)/i, msg: "Makes key lookup case-insensitive" }, { re: /instanceof\s+Date/i, msg: "Formats Date values" }],
    hints: ["Apex Map<String, ...> keys are case-sensitive - build a lower-cased copy of the map first.", "Walk the matches: append the text between the previous end() and this start(), then the value; append the tail after the loop."],
    ai: "Verify whitespace inside braces, case-insensitive keys, unknown/null to empty string, Date formatting, text outside tokens preserved exactly, and that values containing regex special characters such as $ or \\ do not break the merge."
