    id: "AP037",
    track: "apex",
    level: "Hard",
    topic: "OOP",
    title: "Pluggable pricing via Type.forName",
    task: "Thames Logistics stores the pricing strategy class name in config so admins can switch it without a deploy.\n- Interface `PricingStrategy` with `Decimal price(Decimal listPrice, Integer quantity)`\n- `VolumeDiscountStrategy`: 15% off for qty >= 100, 5% for >= 10, else none\n- In `PricingEngine` (inner `PricingConfigException`): `public static PricingStrategy getStrategy(String className)` - instantiate by name with Type.forName; throw PricingConfigException for blank names, unknown classes or classes that don't implement PricingStrategy; cache instances by name (case-insensitive)\n- `public static Decimal quote(String className, Decimal listPrice, Integer quantity)` - 2 dp HALF_UP",
    starter: "public interface PricingStrategy {\n    Decimal price(Decimal listPrice, Integer quantity);\n}\n\npublic with sharing class PricingEngine {\n    public static PricingStrategy getStrategy(String className) {\n        // TODO\n        return null;\n    }\n\n    public static Decimal quote(String className, Decimal listPrice, Integer quantity) {\n        // TODO\n        return null;\n    }\n}\n",
    solution: "public interface PricingStrategy {\n    Decimal price(Decimal listPrice, Integer quantity);\n}\n\npublic with sharing class VolumeDiscountStrategy implements PricingStrategy {\n    public Decimal price(Decimal listPrice, Integer quantity) {\n        Decimal pct = quantity >= 100 ? 0.15 : (quantity >= 10 ? 0.05 : 0);\n        return listPrice * quantity * (1 - pct);\n    }\n}\n\npublic with sharing class PricingEngine {\n    public class PricingConfigException extends Exception {}\n\n    private static final Map<String, PricingStrategy> CACHE = new Map<String, PricingStrategy>();\n\n    public static PricingStrategy getStrategy(String className) {\n        if (String.isBlank(className)) {\n            throw new PricingConfigException('Strategy class name is required');\n        }\n        String key = className.trim().toLowerCase();\n        if (CACHE.containsKey(key)) return CACHE.get(key);\n        Type strategyType = Type.forName(className.trim());\n        if (strategyType == null) {\n            throw new PricingConfigException('Unknown pricing strategy: ' + className);\n        }\n        Object candidate = strategyType.newInstance();\n        if (!(candidate instanceof PricingStrategy)) {\n            throw new PricingConfigException(className + ' does not implement PricingStrategy');\n        }\n        PricingStrategy strategy = (PricingStrategy) candidate;\n        CACHE.put(key, strategy);\n        return strategy;\n    }\n\n    public static Decimal quote(String className, Decimal listPrice, Integer quantity) {\n        return getStrategy(className).price(listPrice, quantity).setScale(2, System.RoundingMode.HALF_UP);\n    }\n}\n",
    checks: [{ re: /Type\.forName\(/i, msg: "Resolves the class with Type.forName" }, { re: /newInstance\(\)/i, msg: "Instantiates with newInstance()" }, { re: /instanceof\s+PricingStrategy/i, msg: "Checks the instance implements PricingStrategy" }, { re: /implements\s+PricingStrategy/i, msg: "VolumeDiscountStrategy implements PricingStrategy" }, { re: /class\s+PricingConfigException\s+extends\s+Exception/i, msg: "Defines PricingConfigException" }],
    hints: ["Type.forName returns null for an unknown class rather than throwing.", "newInstance() returns Object - check instanceof before casting to avoid a TypeException."],
