    level: "Hard",
    topic: "JSON & Transforms",
    title: "Sort shipments with a Comparator",
    task: "Thames Logistics' carrier API returns [{\"ref\":\"TL-1\",\"eta\":\"2026-10-08\",\"weightKg\":12.5,\"currency\":\"GBP\"}]. `currency` is a reserved word in Apex, so it can't be a property name.\nIn class `ShipmentPlanner` create:\n- inner class `Shipment` (ref, Date eta, Decimal weightKg, currencyCode)\n- inner class `ByEtaThenWeight implements Comparator<Shipment>`: eta ascending with null etas last, then weightKg descending (null = 0)\n- `public static List<Shipment> parseAndSort(String body)` - parse (mapping 'currency' -> currencyCode), sort with the comparator; blank -> empty list\n- `public static String toJson(List<Shipment> shipments)` - nulls suppressed, key written back as 'currency'",
    starter: "public with sharing class ShipmentPlanner {\n    public static List<Shipment> parseAndSort(String body) {\n        // TODO\n        return null;\n    }\n\n    public static String toJson(List<Shipment> shipments) {\n        // TODO\n        return null;\n    }\n}\n",
    solution: "public with sharing class ShipmentPlanner {\n    public class Shipment {\n        public String ref;\n        public Date eta;\n        public Decimal weightKg;\n        public String currencyCode;\n    }\n\n    public class ByEtaThenWeight implements Comparator<Shipment> {\n        public Integer compare(Shipment a, Shipment b) {\n            if (a.eta != b.eta) {\n                if (a.eta == null) return 1;\n                if (b.eta == null) return -1;\n                return a.eta < b.eta ? -1 : 1;\n            }\n            Decimal wa = a.weightKg == null ? 0 : a.weightKg;\n            Decimal wb = b.weightKg == null ? 0 : b.weightKg;\n            if (wa == wb) return 0;\n            return wa > wb ? -1 : 1;\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static List<Shipment> parseAndSort(String body) {\n        List<Shipment> shipments = new List<Shipment>();\n        if (String.isBlank(body)) return shipments;\n        for (Object raw : (List<Object>) JSON.deserializeUntyped(body)) {\n            Map<String, Object> row = (Map<String, Object>) raw;\n            Shipment s = new Shipment();\n            s.ref = (String) row.get('ref');\n            String eta = (String) row.get('eta');\n            s.eta = String.isBlank(eta) ? null : Date.valueOf(eta);\n            Object weight = row.get('weightKg');\n            s.weightKg = weight == null ? null : Decimal.valueOf(String.valueOf(weight));\n            s.currencyCode = (String) row.get('currency');\n            shipments.add(s);\n        }\n        shipments.sort(new ByEtaThenWeight());\n        return shipments;\n    }\n\n    public static String toJson(List<Shipment> shipments) {\n        return JSON.serialize(shipments, true).replace('\"currencyCode\":', '\"currency\":');\n    }\n}\n",
