    level: "Hard",
    topic: "Algorithms",
    title: "Top-K complaint categories",
    task: "Thames Logistics' support AI agent summarises the most common complaint types.\nWrite `public static List<String> topCategories(List<Case> cases, Integer k)` in class `ComplaintAnalyser`.\n- Category = Case.Type; skip blank; de-duplicate case-insensitively and ignoring extra spaces ('Late  delivery' = 'late delivery'), displaying the first-seen spelling (spaces normalised)\n- Count occurrences, sort by count desc then label asc (case-insensitive)\n- Return up to k entries formatted '<label> (<count>)'\n- Null/empty cases or k <= 0 return an empty list\n- Use a Map for counting and a Comparable/Comparator for sorting",
    starter: "public with sharing class ComplaintAnalyser {\n    public static List<String> topCategories(List<Case> cases, Integer k) {\n        // TODO\n        return new List<String>();\n    }\n}\n",
    solution: "public with sharing class ComplaintAnalyser {\n    public class CategoryCount implements Comparable {\n        public String label;\n        public Integer total = 0;\n\n        public CategoryCount(String label) {\n            this.label = label;\n        }\n\n        public Integer compareTo(Object other) {\n            CategoryCount that = (CategoryCount) other;\n            if (total != that.total) {\n                return total > that.total ? -1 : 1;\n            }\n            return label.toLowerCase().compareTo(that.label.toLowerCase());\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static List<String> topCategories(List<Case> cases, Integer k) {\n        List<String> result = new List<String>();\n        if (cases == null || cases.isEmpty() || k == null || k <= 0) return result;\n        Map<String, CategoryCount> counts = new Map<String, CategoryCount>();\n        for (Case c : cases) {\n            if (String.isBlank(c.Type)) continue;\n            String display = c.Type.normalizeSpace();\n            String key = display.toLowerCase();\n            CategoryCount entry = counts.get(key);\n            if (entry == null) {\n                entry = new CategoryCount(display);\n                counts.put(key, entry);\n            }\n            entry.total++;\n        }\n        List<CategoryCount> ranked = counts.values();\n        ranked.sort();\n        for (Integer i = 0; i < Math.min(k, ranked.size()); i++) {\n            result.add(ranked[i].label + ' (' + ranked[i].total + ')');\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n}\n",
